From 52ec9f11d8524014edb8361fe706106c01762aa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Armin Le Grand (collabora)" <Armin.LeGrand@collabora.com>
Date: Tue, 5 May 2026 11:46:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CairoSDPR: Improve buffering of huge BitmapData
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

We already did some improvements, but I wanted to clean
this up somewhat. Reason for the needed corrections was
in principle the sqrt()-based general calculation of
the HoldTime in the default implementation of
calculateCombinedHoldCyclesInSeconds. The original idea
was to hold huge data shorter due to memory constraints.
To solve that we added an adapted version to
CairoPixelProcessor2D.

With lessons learned I decided to remove that and
provide a revised general implementation based on linear
scaling of the HoldTime. Based on assuming the seen
huge Bitmap and estimating 20min for it, just create a
factor and multiply with SizeInBytes.

I checked that and it works as intended. It will spare
us from this problem re-occurring with future SDPRs.

NOTE: This still keeps the CairoSDPR-specific avoiding
of buffering of small Bitmaps when these are available
from Bitmap directly. This stays useful and is
Cairo-specific.

Signed-off-by: Armin Le Grand (collabora) <Armin.LeGrand@collabora.com>
Change-Id: I30c7361c6fbfaf0be90be353091cbaf831db5cd2
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.collaboraoffice.com/c/online/+/2005
Tested-by: Jenkins CPCI <releng@collaboraoffice.com>
Reviewed-by: Tomaž Vajngerl <tomaz.vajngerl@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit a3d3ae5e931a04ff5718382ccffe9f16de336a42)
(cherry picked from commit 7550c6ea0bb82f7574e4b974f8d24bd1662a878b)
